NAME
       touch - create empty files or update file times

SYNOPSIS
       touch [OPTION]... FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       touch sets the access and modification times of each FILE to now. A
       FILE that does not exist is created, empty. The second use is the
       common one: touch is the quickest way to make an empty file.

OPTIONS
       -a     Change only the access time.

       -m     Change only the modification time.

       -c, --no-create
              Do not create missing files.

       -d, --date=TIME
              Use TIME (such as '2026-01-15 10:00' or 'yesterday') instead of
              now.

       -t STAMP
              Use a time written as [[CC]YY]MMDDhhmm[.ss].

       -r, --reference=FILE
              Use the times of FILE.

       -h, --no-dereference
              Change a symbolic link itself, not the file it points to.

EXAMPLES
       Create three empty files:

           touch /tmp/a /tmp/b /tmp/c

       Give a file an old date, for testing find -mtime:

           touch -d '10 days ago' /tmp/old.log

SEE ALSO
       stat(1), ls(1), find(1)
